328. Odd Even Linked List

Given the head of a singly linked list, group all the nodes with odd indices together followed by the nodes with even indices, and return the reordered list.
The first node is considered odd, and the second node is even, and so on. Note that the relative order inside both the even and odd groups should remain as it was in the input.

Explanation:

🔹 Problem Understanding: We are given a singly linked list. Our task is to group all nodes at odd positions first, followed by nodes at even positions.

🔹 Core Idea
    Instead of creating new linked lists, we rearrange the pointers of the existing list.
    We maintain two chains while traversing:     👉 One for odd nodes    👉 One for even nodes
    At the end, we simply connect the odd chain to the head of the even chain.

✅ Step 1 — Initialize Pointers

    We create three pointers:
    ListNode odd = head;
    ListNode even = head.next;
    ListNode evenHead = even;

    Why store evenHead?     Because after building the odd list, we must attach its tail to the start of the even list.
    If we don’t save it — we lose access to even nodes.

✅ Step 2 — Traverse and Rearrange
  odd.next = even.next;
  odd = odd.next;
  The odd pointer skips the even node and connects directly to the next odd node. 
  Then we move the odd pointer forward because the tail of the odd list has changed.

  even.next = odd.next;
  even = even.next;
  Now the even pointer skips the odd node and connects to the next even node.
  This builds the even chain simultaneously.

  This is same as odd.next= odd.next.next and even.next= even.next.next
  Basically we are skipping one node right after and going to the alternative node. 
  So both are correct.

✅ Step 3 — Combine Both Lists by connect odd.next to evenHead;
  return head;


Code:

class Solution {
    public ListNode oddEvenList(ListNode head) {
        
        if(head==null || head.next==null){
            return head;
        }

        ListNode odd= head;
        ListNode even = head.next;
        ListNode evenHead = even;

        while(even!=null && even.next!=null){
            odd.next = odd.next.next;
            odd=odd.next;

            even.next=even.next.next;
            even=even.next;
        }

        odd.next = evenHead;

        return head;
    }
}









